  },
  "description": "kube-scheduler leadership, queues, and scheduling latency. Custom dashboard (the Kubernetes project publishes none); metric families verified against kubernetes v1.37.1 sources: scheduler_schedule_attempts_total, scheduler_scheduling_attempt_duration_seconds, scheduler_pending_pods, scheduler_unschedulable_pods, scheduler_preemption_attempts_total (pkg/scheduler/metrics/metrics.go), plus the standard process_ collectors. Leadership comes from kube-state-metrics' kube_lease_owner for the kube-scheduler Lease (k3s registers no leader_election_master_status). k3s runs the component inside the k3s server process: the kube-scheduler ScrapeConfig (apps/kube-control-plane) scrapes every node and keeps only these families, so process_* describe the whole k3s process. API client request counts are left out: the k3s process shares one REST-client registry across every component.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
